# Gorilla 158 rebase: browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css as built on Firefox 158
# The earlier patches of this file do not apply to pristine 158 (superseded in the policy with
# exclude_reason_158); this patch carries the file from the remaining set to the built tree.

diff --git a/browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css b/browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css
index 67773c7421982215171dce0bfc93c3c2c18d7c80..455d05bc31620fb8789a4edabaeee8ca79f0428e 100644
--- a/browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css
+++ b/browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css
@@ -854,4 +854,31 @@ toolbar[keyNav]:not([collapsed], [customizing]) toolbartabstop,
   &:is([gorilla-level="1"], [gorilla-level="2"]) > :is(.toolbarbutton-icon, .toolbarbutton-text) {
     background-color: var(--toolbarbutton-background-color-active);
   }
+
+  /* Its menu in the Gorilla colours: black, with the toolbar's cyan text. Only this menu: the theme forces every
+   * menu to the system colours with !important on purpose (master-redirect.css, "NATIVE CONTEXT MENU & POPUP
+   * RESTORATION"), so only an !important rule this specific can override it here. Without it the menu was the
+   * system grey with the toolbar's cyan text, hard to read. --toolbar-text-color is the theme's cyan (master-redirect.css, COLOR-VALUE CONVERGENCE) (maintainer, 2026-10-04). */
+  > menupopup {
+    appearance: none !important;
+    --panel-background-color: #000000 !important;
+    --panel-text-color: var(--toolbar-text-color, #00ffff) !important;
+    --panel-border-color: var(--toolbar-text-color, #00ffff) !important;
+    background-color: #000000 !important;
+    color: var(--toolbar-text-color, #00ffff) !important;
+
+    menuitem {
+      appearance: none !important;
+      color: inherit !important;
+
+      &[_moz-menuactive] {
+        background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--toolbar-text-color, #00ffff) 25%, transparent) !important;
+      }
+    }
+
+    menuseparator {
+      appearance: none !important;
+      border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--toolbar-text-color, #00ffff) 40%, transparent) !important;
+    }
+  }
 }
